@RoukankenUserHit(ARG)
;the higher intelligence the user' has, the more sanity loss they will get
;if the user's intelligence is less than B, it will not deal any santiy damage to the user.
IF LEVEL_TO_RANK(ABL:ARG:43) >= 3
SETCOLOR C_RED
CALL LC_PRINT(@"The Roukanken hits %PARSE("your",,,ARG)% sanity.", , 2,)
RESETCOLOR
;DEBUGPRINTFORML RoukankenUserHit: Hit %CALLNAME:ARG%'s sanity by {-LEVEL_TO_RANK(ABL:ARG:43)}
CALLF ChangeEndurance(ARG,"orgasmdeny",-LEVEL_TO_RANK(ABL:ARG:43))
CALLF ChangeEndurance(ARG,"charatrauma",1)
ENDIF


; Chariots were the most common classical weapon, but that require horses 
; For melee weapons, it's typically a Spear and Shield. Sometimes a Sword
; Spears were often very long, and used like how Pikes were in the Renaissance, forming a wall that prevents charges by chariots
; In theory other melee weapons like Maces, Morning Stars, Flails, and others can be made, but they weren't

;I think shields are the main thing that will need to be added to accurately represent the classical era
; It has to be in the off-hand slot
; Because of the nature of the battle style

; You require 2 people for just a single column of a shield wall, and they have to be stationed right behind each other
; With the Shield in the front and the very long spear in the back
; So instead we just have a shorter spear and a crescent shield (circular shield with a hole cut out to allow the spear to poke through)
; Can also include a Rectangular Shield which the romans used, and a standard Circular shield which the Persians use

; Also just looked it up, it's a Sarissa (Macedonian) 
; The shorter spear was called a Dory (Doru) by the Greeks



; For Roman Equipment (late classical), there was more weapons
; You got the:
; Pugio (Dagger)
; Gladuis (Infantry Sword)
; Spatha (Calvery Sword)
; Jasta (Short Spear)
; Javelin
; Pilum (Heavy Javelin)
; Bow
; Crossbow
; Plumbatae (Darts)